{# Replaces #quiz once the points goal (and the target percentage, if required) is met. The image is
   served from the panel app's directory read-only -- see the /media mount in app.py.

   This is the payoff for a quiz that takes several minutes, and it used to be three static party
   emoji and a sentence. The finale is now built from pieces CSS can animate individually, which is
   the only reason any of this needs markup rather than a stylesheet:

   * every party emoji is its OWN span, because a single text node cannot be staggered;
   * every digit of every number is its own span, so they fly in from different directions and
     assemble -- "fragments forming numbers";
   * the confetti is a fixed list of glyph / drift / spin / delay tuples (`render._CONFETTI`) rendered
     as inline custom properties -- the drift is a percentage of the CARD, not of the viewport, so the
     party cannot spill past the window edge and scroll the page (it could when the drawer was open,
     which shifts the card's centre right). Fixed rather than random on purpose: the server renders this screen,
     and a reload should show the same party rather than re-rolling it. The offsets are also spread by
     hand, because a formula (`i * 37 % 100`) looks combed rather than scattered.

   Inert without the game-feel toggle: `juice.css` scopes every rule to `body.juice`, so with it off
   this is the same "🎉 and a sentence" as before, in more spans. `aria-hidden` on the decoration --
   a screen reader wants the numbers and the sentence, not sixteen confetti. #}

{# One span per character, numbered, so each can be sent in from somewhere different. `loop.index0`
   rather than anything random, so the assembly is the same on every render. #}
{# The unit lives INSIDE the figure, not beside it: `.finale-stat` is a flex column, so a sibling
   `%` or `s` became its own row under the number. #}
{% macro number(value, cls="", unit="") %}
<span class="figure {{ cls }}">
  {%- for ch in value | string -%}
  <span class="digit" style="--i: {{ loop.index0 }}">{{ ch }}</span>
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if unit %}<span class="figure-unit">{{ unit }}</span>{% endif -%}
</span>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="finale">
  <div class="confetti" aria-hidden="true">
    {% for glyph, drift, spin, step in confetti %}
    <span class="confetti-bit" style="--drift: {{ drift }}%; --spin: {{ spin * 12 }}deg; --i: {{ step }}">{{ glyph }}</span>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <h2 class="celebrate" aria-hidden="true">
    {% for _ in range(3) %}
    <span class="pop" style="--i: {{ loop.index0 }}">🎉</span>
    {% endfor %}
  </h2>

  <p class="celebrate-text">Quiz complete!</p>

  <div class="finale-figures">
    <span class="finale-stat">
      {{ number(points, "big") }}
      <span class="finale-label">points of {{ goal }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="finale-stat">
      {{ number(percentage, unit="%") }}
      <span class="finale-label">{{ correct }} of {{ attempted }} right</span>
    </span>
    <span class="finale-stat">
      {{ number(elapsed, unit="s") }}
      <span class="finale-label">start to finish</span>
    </span>
  </div>

  <p class="celebrate-text">Well done, now take a break&hellip;</p>
  <img src="{{ prefix }}/media/completed.jpeg" alt="cat sleeping next to computer mouse" width="600" />
</div>
